  "mechanism_card": {
    "hypothesis": "R0's 2 px catalogue collar is the only edit in its lineage with a live-positive claim (solo-d28 0.2708 -> pruned 0.2778), so the collar frontier is the one dose-response the entity has measured. Extending the collar by 1.4 px should keep paying while the removed flank dots sit inside the mapped traces' damage zone, and should stop paying once the removed dots are far enough out to be genuine new fault.",
    "mechanism": "Known catalogue pixels are masked pixel-exactly; a dot there earns no T but still pays the 0.2*(S-M) mass term, and a dot beside them is scored only against new-fault truth. Deleting the 3.0-3.4 px shell removes mass whose expected truth credit is low, and re-placing the same count at the maximum marginal R=3 px kernel credit inside region-even 5 km quotas adds coverage where the binary H19-5 support is un-served. Count is held at 37,654 so emitted mass cannot explain a live change.",
    "non_fault_confounder": "H19-5 is binary, so max-marginal placement cannot distinguish a fault ridge from a lithologic contact, a drainage line or a survey-flight artefact; and new-fault truth is explicitly allowed within 300 m of known traces, so the deleted shell may hold real credit. Both confounders push the live change down, not up.",
    "predicted_live_change": "+0.002 DTI (MODEL; bracket -0.008 to +0.013; not a score)",
    "falsifier": "A paired live receipt against R0 with delta <= -0.010 falsifies the collar extension at this radius and, read together with the 3.0 px rungs, ends the outward collar ladder. Any |delta| < 0.010 is no evidence under the session rule and licenses no further dose guess on this axis.",
    "structural_geologist_note": "The deleted shell is a 340 m halo around every mapped trace; the added dots are the least-served parts of the binary H19-5 field, which is not a fault-probability ranking. Read the file as a collar test with a repaired refill, not as a claim that new faults avoid mapped traces."
  },
